# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FG-Metal — published scope
#
# This repository publishes the library, its documentation, the round reports
# cited by that documentation, and the source of the experiment harness.
#
# The accumulated engineering record — historical round reports, gate
# evidence, instrument traces, and raw captures — is archived on the machine
# that produced it and is deliberately not tracked. It runs to tens of
# gigabytes against a few megabytes of source, which made the repository
# unreadable and slow to clone without making any claim more verifiable: the
# reports that cite that evidence state what was measured, and the evidence is
# retained locally with the run that produced it.
#
# Rules below apply to untracked files only. A file already tracked keeps
# working normally. To publish an excluded artefact deliberately, use
# `git add -f <path>`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Local archive ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything this project retains but does not publish lives under `archive/`,
# grouped by what it is rather than left loose at the root. See the header
# above for why none of it is tracked.
/archive/

# ── Build and tool output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/build/
/build-*/
/cmake-build-*/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
compile_commands.json
build.ninja
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcuserdata/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Generated benchmark output.
/test-results/

# ── Model assets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Weights are fetched and converted locally; copyrighted checkpoints and
# generated runtime weights stay out of Git history.
/models/local/
/models/cache/

# ── Local scratch and agent workspace state ──────────────────────────────────
/.workbuddy-ai/

# ── Experiment evidence trees ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every investigation keeps its report and its harness source in Git, and its
# evidence directory on disk. Evidence is reproducible from the harness and
# the run parameters recorded in the report.
/experiments/*/evidence/
/experiments/*/runs/

# Archived investigation trees. These routes were closed or deferred; their
# reports, audits, patches, and manifests are retained under `archive/`.
# Harness source that the published documentation still cites stays tracked,
# and tracked files are unaffected by these rules.
/experiments/dxgi_public_attachment/
/experiments/dxgi_public_probe/
/experiments/dxmt_framegen/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11a/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11b/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11b1/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11c/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11c1/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11c1r/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11c1r2/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11d3a/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11d3b/
/experiments/dxvk_macos_step11dR/
/experiments/metalfx_fi_capability_probe_R92/
/experiments/storage/

# Raw GPU frame dumps, captured frames, and built observers from the MetalFX
# title-integration rounds: tens of gigabytes per round.
/experiments/metalfx_frame_interpolator_R93/*.dylib
/experiments/metalfx_frame_interpolator_R93/provider_smoke
/experiments/metalfx_frame_interpolator_R93/frame_interpolator_smoke

# Per-round evidence corpora for the live title-integration rounds (observer
# logs, frame captures, PNG captures, built dylibs, launch preparations, build
# directories). Each round's report is published under docs/reports/; the
# corpus stays on the machine that produced it.
/experiments/metalfx_frame_interpolator_R93/r1[0-9][0-9]-evidence/
/experiments/metalfx_frame_interpolator_R93/r127-alpha-runtime/evidence/
